# Prompt to generate the system

You are an advanced life management system architect. Your task is to design a fully integrated, structured, and scalable personal operating system.
The system must function as a centralized dashboard with 4 main sections:
PLANNER
JOURNAL
RESOURCES
FINANCE
All sections must be interconnected, logically structured, printable, and usable digitally (Notion-compatible structure preferred).
────────────────────────
I. MASTER DASHBOARD STRUCTURE
────────────────────────
Create a clean homepage dashboard with 4 main selectable tabs:
• Planner
• Journal
• Resources
• Finance
Each tab should have clear navigation to its internal pages.
Ensure alignment across all systems (goals, habits, finances, ideas).
────────────────────────
II. PLANNER SECTION
────────────────────────
Include previously defined components:
Yearly Overview (12-month calendar)
Yearly Goals Master Tab
Top 3 Goals
4 Sub-goals each
Challenges
Resolution strategies
Vision Board
Monthly Dashboard (12 pages)
Weekly Planning System
Quarterly Reflection Pages
Empty Sketch Page
Ensure goal alignment:
Vision → Yearly Goals → Monthly → Weekly → Daily Top 3
Habit tracking must flow:
Weekly Input → Monthly Dashboard → Quarterly Average
────────────────────────
III. JOURNAL SECTION
────────────────────────
A. Daily Journal Page Template
Include:
Date
Mood indicator
Top 3 Intentions
Main Reflection Entry
Lessons Learned
Gratitude Section
Improvement Note
Rating of the Day (1–10)
B. Journal Tracker (Dashboard View)
Create a tracking page that includes:
Streak counter
Monthly consistency percentage
Mood trend summary
Most common lesson themes
Reflection frequency per month
Design it to:
Identify emotional patterns
Track personal growth
Connect insights to Planner goals
────────────────────────
IV. RESOURCES TRACKER SECTION
────────────────────────
Purpose:
Capture insights from social media, books, podcasts, courses, or conversations and convert them into actionable ideas or lesson plans.
Create a structured Resource Database with the following fields:
Core Fields:
Source Type (Social Media, Book, Podcast, Article, etc.)
Platform / Creator
Topic Category
Insight Summary
Why It Matters
Possible Application (Idea / Lesson Plan / Strategy)
Related Goal (linked to Planner goals)
Action Step
Priority Level
Status (Captured / Developing / Implemented / Archived)
Add Two Functional Views:
Idea Incubator View
Shows insights not yet developed
Focus on turning insights into execution
Lesson Plan Builder View
Structured template:
• Core Concept
• Learning Objective
• Key Takeaways
• Application Exercise
• Supporting Materials
Ensure this tracker transforms passive consumption into active output.
────────────────────────
V. FINANCE TRACKER SECTION
────────────────────────
Create Finance Dashboard with the following sub-pages:
Net Worth Tracker
Assets
Liabilities
Monthly Net Worth Change
Growth Chart
Monthly Expense Tracker
Income
Fixed Expenses
Variable Expenses
Savings Rate
Investment Contribution
Budgeting Tracker (Goal-Based Budgeting)
Create individual budgeting sub-pages for money-required goals such as:
CFA Exam
Master's Degree
Certifications
Major Purchases
Each budgeting page must include:
Total Target Cost
Current Savings
Monthly Allocation
Remaining Gap
Target Deadline
Travel Fund Tracker
Destination
Budget Required
Current Savings
Funding Plan
Retirement Tracker
Target Retirement Age
Required Corpus
Current Investment Value
Monthly Investment Rate
Estimated Growth Projection
Financial Freedom Tracker
Annual Living Expense
Target Passive Income
Current Passive Income
Gap to Freedom
Milestone Progress Bar
Ensure all finance sections:
Align with yearly and life goals
Connect to budgeting and savings strategy
Encourage measurable progress
────────────────────────
SYSTEM DESIGN REQUIREMENTS
────────────────────────
Everything must connect:
Resources → Planner Goals
Planner Goals → Financial Allocation
Journal Insights → Habit Adjustments
Finance → Life Vision
Include dashboard summaries:
Goal Completion %
Habit Consistency %
Financial Progress %
Idea Execution Rate %
Structure must be:
Clean
Action-oriented
Measurable
Scalable
Minimal but powerful
Output format:
Organized template layout
Clear headings
Structured database-style design
Suitable for digital or printable use
Design this as a high-performance personal operating system.

